__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# DESI raw survey data: large FITS files fetched from the official public
# DR1 release are never committed (spec: "repository must remain
# reproducible without embedding tens or hundreds of gigabytes of
# external survey data"). Only small derived/validated fixtures, metadata,
# manifests, and checksums under data/desi/dr1/fc005/{validated,metadata}/
# are tracked -- see download_desi_fc005.py, which re-fetches raw/ from
# the manifest URLs on demand. The one intentionally-committed pilot
# fixture lives under data/desi/dr1/fc005/validated/pilot_fixture/ and is
# explicitly un-ignored below.
data/desi/dr1/fc005/raw/*
!data/desi/dr1/fc005/raw/.gitkeep
data/desi/dr1/fc005/derived/*
!data/desi/dr1/fc005/derived/.gitkeep
!data/desi/dr1/fc005/validated/pilot_fixture/

# External literature PDFs (arXiv preprints, third-party copyrighted
# academic sources downloaded for L0 literature-ingestion phases): never
# committed, same policy as raw DESI survey data above. SHA256 checksums,
# page counts, and full provenance are recorded in
# literature/manifests/*.json/*.md, and every extracted equation/structure
# is preserved with page-level citation in literature/extraction/ and
# literature/crosswalk/ -- so the ingestion is reproducible and auditable
# without embedding the source PDFs themselves.
literature/string_theory/*.pdf
literature/superstring_theory/*.pdf
literature/standard_model/*.pdf
literature/gauge_theory/*.pdf
literature/gauge_theory/*.html
